{
  "rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last ~5–10 days show a clear upswing, the model systematically forecasts too low across almost the entire 30d horizon (level bias). Apply an upward level shift that grows with horizon.",
    "Horizon-amplified bias: the underprediction increases with lead time (small error in days 1–3, large error by days 10–30). Use a lead-time scaling factor (e.g., add a progressively larger premium beyond ~day 5).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the model reacts too slowly to regime changes (breakout from mid-60s to 70s/80s). Incorporate recent slope/acceleration (e.g., 5d vs 20d momentum) to boost the path when momentum is positive.",
    "Systematic ceiling/anchoring: forecasts appear anchored near ~68–71 even when realized prices re-rate into mid/high 70s and low 80s. If price breaks above recent range/high, relax the cap and allow higher trajectory (range-break adjustment).",
    "Missing volatility expansion after breakout: after a sharp rise, the model predicts mild mean reversion/flatness, but outcomes continue trending higher with larger swings. Increase both drift and variance assumptions following a breakout (post-breakout drift uplift)."
  ]
}
